\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.9}{\ignorespaces Snapshots displaying the tensile instability in the perturbation SPH formulation. Even though this formulation was unable to capture the mountain wave dynamics, the terrain arguably introduces an irregularity in the flow. This loss of regularity might trigger the tensile instability, as visible in the particle clumping (left). The clumping triggers a sudden, explosion-like divergence in the maximum velocity (right).}}{95}{figure.caption.103}\protected@file@percent }
